h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.8 (build 691)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Reopen where you were after a crash.</b> While a window has media open, Asobi quietly keeps a recovery copy of its session. If the app quits unexpectedly &#8212; a crash, a force-quit, a power cut &#8212; the next launch offers to reopen the same clips at the clip and frame you were on, with the notes, marks, grades and trims made up to a few seconds before. Your own session file is never touched; what comes back is unsaved until you save it.</li>
<li><b>Resume hosting.</b> If that window was hosting a review, a second button brings the same room back, so the links people already have keep working and guests in a browser reconnect on their own.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
